      "mergeID": "6740e47133cdb93357c9a42c",
      "mergedPostDetails": "This doesn't happen to my Samsung Galaxy S21 Ultra but I'm experiencing this issue on my new Samsung Galaxy S24 Ultra. I often use Samsung Galaxy Buds+. Exceptions where this does not happen is turning off the device screen. The steps to replicate this bug goes as follows:\n\n1. Make sure that the Bluetooth headphones or earbuds are connected to the device.\n\n2. Open the VRChat application and press the play button. Wait until you join the world.\n\n3. Unfocus the application by doing actions that make it leave the app without fully closing, such as pressing the home button for example, but don't let it fully close by itself if left running for too long in the background. \n\n4. Switch back to the app to focus. The game audio will suddenly disappear and the mic will stop working, resulting in the mic not picking up audio.\n\nNot every compatible device might be able to reproduce this bug.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1535] Game audio and mic immediately stops working if you unfocus the app while using Bluetooth headphones/earbuds in some Android devices",
